   precompiler Mapbox ships (style._programPrecompiler) only runs on 'idle', after those frames, and skips circle and symbol layers.  GTBG_PRECOMPILE(map) queues every
   program of the current style (plus the circle and text-SDF symbol programs) right after the style or its layers changed, so the GPU process links them in parallel
   while tiles load; with {terrain: true} it then queues the terrain (and terrain + fog) variants in idle slices, before anybody asks for terrain.
   GTBG_PRECOMPILE_TERRAIN(map) is the second part alone.  Both use only fields
   of the SRI-pinned mapbox-gl.js v3.24.1 and do nothing (inside try/catch) when a field is missing or KHR_parallel_shader_compile is absent. */
